{"id":"h132","run":2,"role":"calibration","category":"claim","question":"Is the following claim true? The first transatlantic telegraph cable was completed in 1838.","truth":"no","model_answer":"no","correct":true,"source":"author-written for this project; verified by the author","claims":[{"text":"The first transatlantic telegraph cable was laid in 1858, not 1838.","confidence":0.97,"lean":-1,"theta":1.5237,"phi":2.8104},{"text":"The Atlantic Telegraph Company under Cyrus Field completed a working Ireland–Newfoundland cable in August 1858.","confidence":0.95,"lean":-1,"theta":1.4923,"phi":2.9965},{"text":"The 1858 cable carried messages for only a few weeks before failing.","confidence":0.93,"lean":0.0,"theta":1.4608,"phi":2.9563},{"text":"A more durable transatlantic cable followed in 1866.","confidence":0.93,"lean":-1,"theta":1.4608,"phi":3.0945},{"text":"In 1838 the Cooke and Wheatstone telegraph was in use on the Great Western Railway.","confidence":0.9,"lean":-1,"theta":1.4137,"phi":-2.2085},{"text":"Wheatstone discussed the idea of an Atlantic crossing in 1838, but no cable was made or laid.","confidence":0.88,"lean":-1,"theta":1.3823,"phi":2.7639},{"text":"There are no substantive considerations supporting the 1838 claim.","confidence":0.9,"lean":-1,"theta":1.4137,"phi":2.5928},{"text":"The only link to 1838 is that telegraphy was being developed and an Atlantic crossing was discussed as a possibility.","confidence":0.85,"lean":1,"theta":1.3352,"phi":1.8019},{"text":"No transatlantic cable existed in 1838, so the claim is false.","confidence":0.97,"lean":-1,"theta":1.5237,"phi":2.7631}],"relations":[{"i":0,"j":1,"J":0.8,"relation":"supports"},{"i":0,"j":2,"J":0.3,"relation":"supports"},{"i":0,"j":5,"J":0.6,"relation":"supports"},{"i":0,"j":6,"J":0.5,"relation":"supports"},{"i":0,"j":7,"J":0.4,"relation":"supports"},{"i":0,"j":8,"J":0.9,"relation":"supports"},{"i":1,"j":2,"J":0.4,"relation":"supports"},{"i":1,"j":3,"J":0.2,"relation":"supports"},{"i":2,"j":3,